From e8efacd0a7b0eb222c597fd43e6790860fd8f795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:26:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] docs: the system-prompt cache works under a layer split
 too

FLAGS.md, DETAILS.md and SPILL_AND_PROMPT_CACHE.md still said the function runs
on a single session and does not work with --layer-split.  It does: one session
file per stage under the variant's key and a joint sidecar that carries the stage
count (sidecar version 2; a version 1 single file is still read), and a variant
stored while part of the context lived in host RAM loads back.  The --mtp
requirement stands: without MTP the feature reports itself off.
---
 docs/DETAILS.md                | 6 ++++--
 docs/FLAGS.md                  | 2 +-
 docs/SPILL_AND_PROMPT_CACHE.md | 8 ++++++--
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

